@flexiarg creativity-commons/process-fits-local-conditions
@title Process Fits Local Conditions
@keywords congruence, local conditions, embedded evaluation, grammatisation, Ostrom 2A
@audience Producers, agent packet authors
@tone normative
@style pattern
@grade principle
@provenance Ostrom design principle 2A (congruence with local conditions), as transposed in Corneli 2016 (ICCC 2016), Table 2 and section "2A. Congruence with local conditions" (Winnicott's interweave; Clark; Stiegler's grammatisation). Drafted by claude-16 with Joe, 2026-10-29. Derived from the paper, not mined from runs.
@transposes institutions/congruence-with-local-conditions
@status draft 2026-10-29; runs correct it
@references [creativity-commons/ARGUMENT creativity-commons/place-boundaries creativity-commons/distributed-monitoring]

! conclusion:
  The Process is related to local conditions: the Producer reads the
  Place (its time, place, technology and quantity of resource units)
  and uses existing artefacts there to evaluate its own work as it goes.

  + context:
    Local conditions live in the interweave of Place and Producer. While
    a Producer makes sense of the Place, others in the Place are making
    sense of the Producer.

  + IF:
    A Producer brings a general method into a particular Place.

  + HOWEVER:
    Reading the Place costs time, and a Producer that only conforms
    stops contributing anything the Place did not already have
    ("program or be programmed").

  + THEN:
    Before acting, parse the Place: its conventions, its existing tests,
    its record of past decisions. Use those artefacts as an embedded
    evaluation (how close is my output to what is already accepted here,
    and where does it differ on purpose). Record where you departed from
    local convention and why.

  + BECAUSE:
    Rules and products that ignore local conditions get rejected or
    ignored, whatever their general merit. Embedded evaluation turns the
    Place's own artefacts into the Producer's sensorium.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Example: an Emacs fix reads the bug thread, the library's existing ERT suite and the ChangeLog commit style before writing code.]
    next[Candidate source of local conditions: closed debbugs threads record how maintainers actually decided; mine them as patterns.]
